{"agent_id":"anon-ab6221f8","agent_seq":24,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T06:41:14.906908506Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f306b1ce-013d-4108-bf01-8b3855cd5301","comment_uuid":"5f596b4f-a440-47d7-88e2-2b53a4f56147","author":"anon-ab6221f8","content":"[action] Review origin/develop architecture: boundaries, persistence, agent providers, failure modes, alternatives, and migration path","created_at":"2026-08-19T06:41:14.906902684Z","kind":"note"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-ab6221f8","agent_seq":25,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T06:46:40.236287084Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f306b1ce-013d-4108-bf01-8b3855cd5301","comment_uuid":"e14c0492-71a5-449c-95dd-723f0b999cf2","author":"anon-ab6221f8","content":"Architecture review of origin/develop 35255a17 complete. Verdict: changes required. Preserve Rust, per-agent Git refs, signed domain events, SQLite projections, worktree isolation, and provider invocation IR. Replace the global timestamp watermark with per-agent causal frontiers; stop rewriting whole events.log and checkpoint state per mutation; make every CLI/API/TUI/orchestrator mutation use one application service and fail closed; project incrementally into SQLite; use remote CAS refs for authoritative online locks; eliminate the v3 cache worktree; split the 94k-line duplicate lib/bin module tree into a modular workspace; consolidate hooks/MCP into binary subcommands and generate provider assets from one canonical bundle. Current high-risk evidence includes direct SQLite-only REST/orchestrator writes, silent SharedWriter fallback, global-watermark late-event loss, scalar checkpoint adoption, warning-only signature validation, forced dashboard wildcard fetch, and full-state hydration per write.","created_at":"2026-08-19T06:46:40.235900269Z","kind":"result"}}
