{"agent_id":"anon-ab6221f8","agent_seq":28,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T06:57:28.954418660Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f306b1ce-013d-4108-bf01-8b3855cd5301","comment_uuid":"80a19efe-f6b3-4c5c-9971-1ee611b75841","author":"anon-ab6221f8","content":"Recommended audit sequence: first establish non-negotiable invariants and a system-level authority/data-flow map; then audit vertically by subsystem rather than alphabetically file-by-file, recording every finding in a living Markdown ledger with severity, evidence, violated invariant, callers, migration risk, recommended disposition, and verification. Do not begin with broad cruft deletion because compatibility, migration, generated-provider, and live enforcement paths are interleaved. Prioritize storage/reducer/sync, all mutation consumers, hooks/providers, workflows, dashboard/server, config/assets, then legacy/build/tests. Convert coherent finding clusters into separately deliverable refactor designs.","created_at":"2026-08-19T06:57:28.954406979Z","kind":"decision"}}
