{"agent_id":"anon-ab6221f8","agent_seq":31,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T07:15:35.884813080Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f306b1ce-013d-4108-bf01-8b3855cd5301","comment_uuid":"4e0f66a9-b48b-476c-b172-2589d059adf7","author":"anon-ab6221f8","content":"Completed the repository-grounded overhead map at .design/crosslink-architecture-overhead-map.md on docs/crosslink-architecture-overhead-map, audited against origin/develop 35255a17. It maps runtime surfaces, all primary durable state families, write/sync/reduce/hydrate flows, mutation bypasses, hooks/providers, kickoff/swarm/orchestrator/pipeline duplication, dashboards, external trust boundaries, compatibility, failure recovery, 17 prioritized pressure points, and a 9-phase refactor sequence. Core direction preserves Git-native shared authority, local-only SQLite projection, and mandatory provider hooks.","created_at":"2026-08-19T07:15:35.884809117Z","kind":"result"}}
